oday can be expressed in terms of its initial height \\(h\\) and the growth factor over \\(14\\) days:\n\\[ 452 = h \\times (1.05)^{14} \\]\n\nTo find \\(h\\), we need to solve for \\(h\\):\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{(1.05)^{14}} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate \\((1.05)^{14}\\):\n\\[ (1.05)^{14} \\approx 1.9799 \\]\n\nNow, substitute this value back into the equation:\n\\[ h = \\frac{452}{1.9799} \\approx 228.2 \\]\n\nRounding to the nearest tenth, we get:\n\\[ h \\approx 228.2 \\]\n\nThus, the height of the plant two weeks ago was \\(\\boxed{228.2}\\) cm."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{228.2}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:1177"}
